{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And he said, Send me.</b> The angel was afraid to leave without permission, lest they punish him from Heaven with bolts of fire, since he had come to wrestle with him on a mission from the Holy One, blessed be He; therefore he considered himself bound, and he entreated him and said, 'Send me,' in the manner of what is written (Hosea 12:5): ״וישר אל מלאך ויוכל בכה ויתחנן לו״." "<b>For the dawn has risen.</b> Jacob said to him: Are you a thief or a tax-collector that you are afraid of the dawn? He said to him: I am no thief and no tax-collector, but an angel; and from the day I was created my time to recite song has not arrived until now. Therefore he informed him that it is the time of the recitation of song for angels, as it is written (Job 38:7): ״ברן יחד כוכבי בוקר ויריעו כל בני אלהים״. It is the time of sanctification, as is said (Isaiah 6): ״וקרא זה אל זה ואמר״. And Jacob answered him: <b>I will not let you go unless you bless me.</b> — that you should testify to me concerning the blessings with which my father blessed me. And he said to him: <b>No longer shall your name be called Jacob, but Israel.</b> That is to say, the blessings are given to you in the mode of עקבה only in dominion and judgment; or: you deceived Laban, but in truth and wholeness you did what you did. Therefore the attribute of truth was given him, to say that he was truthful in all his words and in all his deeds, as it is written (Micah 7:20): ״תתן אמת ליעקב״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:17:18.825407104Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}